    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_aee375bf5573cffe9a305bd94ffb6fd4101fcc7b10726b22f00c60eb4eefddfb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source examines the same freezing proposal through complementary representations: normalized zeta maxima test the predicted location, fluctuation density, and tail, whereas exponentiating the zeta log-modulus creates a β-indexed partition function whose normalized free energy tests the predicted phase-transition curve and frozen plateau.",
